WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.326
Start continuity analysis with the process, not the server list.

00:00:05.326 --> 00:00:19.453
Identify which physical outputs and services are essential, what minimum capacity is acceptable, how long interruption can be tolerated, and which conditions require safe shutdown rather than continued operation.

00:00:19.453 --> 00:00:24.316
Map each process to the assets that enable it.

00:00:24.316 --> 00:00:27.327
PLCs and RTUs execute control.

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:32.190
HMIs and SCADA systems provide operator visibility and commands.

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:34.274
Historians preserve trends.

00:00:34.274 --> 00:00:38.211
Engineering workstations hold configuration and programming capability.

00:00:38.211 --> 00:00:44.464
Networks, time services, identity, remote access, and security controls connect the environment.

00:00:44.464 --> 00:00:47.474
Dependencies extend beyond cyber assets.

00:00:47.474 --> 00:01:00.211
Electrical power, backup generation, cooling, compressed air, water, fuel, communications, buildings, field instrumentation, spare parts, specialized tools, and trained personnel may determine whether recovery is possible.

00:01:00.211 --> 00:01:08.780
Vendor and supply-chain dependencies matter when equipment requires proprietary software, licenses, firmware, support credentials, or replacement modules.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:13.643
Record contract contacts, response times, shipping constraints, and alternatives.

00:01:13.643 --> 00:01:20.822
A spare is only useful if it is compatible and can be configured safely.

00:01:20.822 --> 00:01:27.075
Build a dependency map that shows prerequisites and single points of failure.

00:01:27.075 --> 00:01:36.107
A redundant server may still depend on one switch, one power source, one storage system, or one engineer.

00:01:36.107 --> 00:01:43.286
Include upstream and downstream processes so local recovery does not create a larger imbalance.

00:01:43.286 --> 00:01:48.612
Use the map to set restoration priorities and recovery packages.

00:01:48.612 --> 00:01:54.865
Validate it with operators, engineers, maintenance, safety, IT, security, facilities, and vendors.

00:01:54.865 --> 00:02:04.360
Architecture documents should describe the system the organization actually operates, then be updated after every significant change or exercise.
